<p>It&#8217;s the news everyone was expecting, but now it&#8217;s official: Apple has <a href="https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/ted-lasso-season-5-renewed-apple-tv-jason-sudeikis-1236956126/">renewed &#8220;Ted Lasso&#8221; for another season</a>, reports Variety:</p>
<blockquote><p>
  Believe: “<a href="https://variety.com/t/ted-lasso/">Ted Lasso</a>” and the Lady Greyhounds are back for more. <a href="https://variety.com/t/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> announced Monday that it has given a Season 5 pickup to the hit <a href="https://variety.com/t/jason-sudeikis/">Jason Sudeikis</a> comedy from Warner Bros. TV.</p>
<p>  News wasn’t a surprise, given how well the Season 4 revival did for Apple TV; it just came down to striking a new deal with Sudeikis and Warner Bros. to continue the show. Sudeikis is back as star and executive producer. On a <a href="https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/jason-sudeikis-wants-ted-lasso-season-5-olivia-wilde-split-1236916062/">recent episode</a> of the podcast “Talk Easy With Sam Fragoso,” Sudeikis expressed an interest in continuing “Ted Lasso” through Seasons 5 and 6, making for another three-season arc.
</p></blockquote>
<p>I thought <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/08/review-ted-lasso-returns-to-the-pitch/">the new season was pretty good</a>, and hoped that Apple would <a href="https://www.theincomparable.com/theincomparable/840/">back up the money truck</a> to Jason Sudeikis&#8217;s house for more seasons. Here we are.</p>
<p>It was previously reported that the show was <a href="https://mastodon.screentimes.net/@sigmund/117151079443786779">planning to shoot in the UK starting in January</a>, another sign that this announcement was just a matter of timing.</p>
